  "supersedes": {
    "suite": "01",
    "freeze": "evidence/s2_r3_context_suite_20261016/suite_freeze.json",
    "why": [
      "POST_PHONE_15 was a single FIT-signer snippet selected by the reference model's own POST state: circular and single-source, so it is now diagnostic only.",
      "Held-out decomposition showed hands held at the sign-end position is the dominant continuous failure; v01 had no hold condition.",
      "False activations under a preceding non-sign history were not measured in v01.",
      "Tier-2 mixed paused isolated sessions with continuous ones; continuous sessions are now gated separately and signer roles recorded.",
      "signs-with-event credited one merged episode to two signs; v02 gates one-to-one distinct events and merged-event count."
    ],
    "frozen_before_any_s2_r3_training": true
  },
  "tier1_raw_conditions": "raw_* conditions stitch genuine raw-v1 at the RAW level and recompute features over the joined sequence (no start-of-sequence marker). HOLD_g: previous clip of the same held-out signer and cadence (first other clip in manifest order) up to its last ACTIVE observation, that observation held for g observations (diagnostic-only duplication), then the target from one observation before its first ACTIVE. Hold rows are not scored as false activations (label ambiguous). Session histories use the last `length` rows of the source interval; confirmed non-sign rows are scored for history false ACTIVE.",
  "gate_rationale": "Absolute acquisition targets are set near isolated-sign performance (NONE 0.986); recall after non-sign movement must reach ~80% of isolated recall (0.869). False activations are non-inferiority against the frozen S2-R2 reference. Thresholds were fixed before any S2-R3 model existed."
